Short answer

Hydra columnar compresses data at the chunk level: each column's "value buffer" for a chunk is (optionally) compressed when the chunk is serialized. The null/exists bitmap (existsBuffer) is kept uncompressed and the compressed value buffers are written into the stripe section of the data file. Decompression happens per chunk when that chunk is read.
